+            "",
+            f"Passenger queue (run-length notation): (R^{inst['target']} G^{inst['target']})^{inst['n']}.",
+            "Thus the displayed pair of runs repeats exactly the stated number of times.",
+            "",
+            f"Give a clearing schedule as exactly {inst['n']} triples of path IDs. For each",
+            "triple, dispatch all still-red buses from its three paths, in any order, followed",
+            "by all green buses from those same paths. Process the triples in the listed order.",
+            "Every path ID must occur exactly once. IDs are zero-based; repetitions are forbidden.",
+            "The order of triples and the order of IDs within a triple do not affect validity.",
+            "",
+            "Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as a JSON array of",
+            f"exactly {inst['n']} arrays, each containing exactly three integer path IDs.",
+            "Syntax example for a hypothetical six-path instance:",
+            "<answer>[[0,2,4],[1,3,5]]</answer>",
